(2170073, 295742, 48228, '<td valign="top">I learned so much from this image and this challenge..... I see the mistakes that I have made, and hopefully will learn from them..... <br/> <br/>Remember this is only my second challenge entry. <br/>I have read all the comments, and found them to be very helpfull, so Thank-you everyone.....</td>', 'I learned so much from this image and this challenge..... I see the mistakes that I have made, and hopefully will learn from them.....  Remember this is only my second challenge entry. I have read all the comments, and found them to be very helpfull, so Thank-you everyone.....', '2006-02-22 03:43:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2170112, 294087, 52472, '<td valign="top">I know, it looks a bit grey and blurred. I thought it could pass as a touch of heaven or something like that, but not a lot seemed to see it this way. I used a flash for lighting up the face and a reflector bound to a thin thread, rotating around her head and illuminated by a weak halogen lamp. This was my mistake because I set the white balance on flashlight and the portrait had a strong yellow cast. When I corrected that on the computer, the hallow was barely visible anymore and I had to apply a lot of filters which gave this blurr and greyish tone!<br/> <br/>If I have ever again to make a picture of a halo again, I will rotate a light source instead of a reflector and it should work fine.</td>', 'I know, it looks a bit grey and blurred. I thought it could pass as a touch of heaven or something like that, but not a lot seemed to see it this way. I used a flash for lighting up the face and a reflector bound to a thin thread, rotating around her head and illuminated by a weak halogen lamp. This was my mistake because I set the white balance on flashlight and the portrait had a strong yellow cast. When I corrected that on the computer, the hallow was barely visible anymore and I had to apply a lot of filters which gave this blurr and greyish tone! If I have ever again to make a picture of a halo again, I will rotate a light source instead of a reflector and it should work fine.', '2006-02-22 04:18:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2170151, 295755, 22781, '<td valign="top">Who else could this be :)<br/> <br/>Congrats again...</td>', 'Who else could this be :) Congrats again...', '2006-02-22 04:39:33.000000', NULL, 0),
